# The names of Unicode 17.0.0: every name the database lists, written as
# words of `WORD_TEXT`; the ranges whose names a rule makes; the aliases; the
# named sequences; and an index of every name, alias and named sequence by
# the hash of its loose form, UAX #44's rule LM2, in buckets.
#
# The table is data, made and not typed: a one-off program read the Unicode
# Character Database 17.0.0 (UCD.zip of https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/,
# fetched 2026-11-17), packed it, held the name the packed tables give every
# one of the 1,114,112 code points to Python 3.15.2's `unicodedata.name`
# (17.0.0), and every name, alias and named sequence looked up through the
# index to `unicodedata.lookup`, then wrote this module
# whole. Nothing here is edited by hand. What it read:
